Marathon data for Aleph One
===========================

Aleph One is the engine only: it comes with no game. Bungie released the
data of Marathon, Marathon 2: Durandal and Marathon Infinity for free
distribution, and the Aleph One project hosts it at

    https://alephone.lhowon.org/

Take the "data" archive of each scenario (Marathon-20230529-Data.zip,
Marathon2-20230529-Data.zip, MarathonInfinity-20230529-Data.zip, or the
same release as this program), not an installer for another system. Each
unpacks to a drawer holding Map, Shapes, Sounds, Images, Music (or a
Music drawer) and Scripts/MML/Plugins drawers of its own.

Then either

  - copy the CONTENTS of one scenario's drawer into the Scenario drawer
    here, and open AlephOne's icon; or

  - keep the scenarios where you like, and name one when you start:

        AlephOne Work:Games/Marathon2

    or, from Workbench, set the DATA tool type of AlephOne's icon
    (Icons, Information..., tool types) to DATA=Work:Games/Marathon2 (one
    is there, in brackets: take the brackets off), or shift-click the
    scenario's drawer and then AlephOne's icon.

Preferences, saved games, films and screenshots go in a User drawer
beside the program, made on the first run.

The scenario data is not included here and must not be packaged with this
port: it is Bungie's, distributed by the Aleph One project.
